source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: The first `|` ends the image source even directly after a backslash, so the source keeps the backslash and the rest becomes a parameter.
-- input.jira --
!http://x/i\|b.png!
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="http://x/i\" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>
-- want.md --
!http://x/i\\|b.png!
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 14,
  "Construct": "image",
  "Reason": "Jira image parameter name cannot be represented by JFM attribute grammar; complete image remains literal"
 }
]
